    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d286">

                <pb facs="0463" n="367" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg367"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1898-05-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 9, 1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 383.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that I
                    received a note this morning from the foreign office, dated the 7th instant,
                    transmitting an extract from a telegram to Her Majesty’s secretary of state for
                    the colonies from the governor of Sierra Leone, reporting the death of certain
                    American missionaries at the hand of the insurgents in that colony and
                    mentioning others as being safe at Freetown, of both of which I inclose herewith
                    copies.</p>
                <p>I beg also to inclose herewith a copy of your telegraphic instruction, together
                    with my telegraphic reply thereto, both of this date and relative to the above
                    subject.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>






